      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_root_prev_coef_window_initialized_before_latch_copy",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "On the first progressive Huffman scan, this loop has no `else` initialization for `prev_coef_bit_ptr[coefi]` when `input_scan_number == 1`. The step therefore leaves each component's `prev_coef_bits[1..9]` undefined even though later block-smoothing code assumes those previous-scan entries are initialized. The fix patch adds `else prev_coef_bit_ptr[coefi] = 0;` at this exact site; the recovered witness JPEG uses `SOF2`/`FFC4`, so the `jdphuff.c` side of the patch is the executed root cause."
    },
